was wasted  potential that such an interesting plot  point never ended up affecting the  finale for that reason in an anime  original ending it'd be interesting to  see aaron using this royal baby to  reactivate the rumbling and there's one  realistic way it can happen if we flash  back to when the jager bros first made  contact there was a good five to ten  seconds where a huge lightning bolt  shoots down into shiganchina during that  moment eric had done the same thing as  lara tiber and essentially used the  lightning as a conduit to send himself  on the ground while underground he could  then encase himself in a crystal in  exactly the same way she did and he  could stay in this position until his  body fully regenerates on top of that he  could then remotely control his massive  titan on the surface by using the  warhammer cable and remember since this  cable is made from titan hardening the  founder can keep extending it for  literally as long as he needs to it's  highly unlikely that anyone in  shiganshin would even notice if he did  this considering they'd be too  distracted by the falling debris pure  titans and politics giving aaron all the  time he needs to put things in place as  the founder he could easily control one  of zeke's titans and make them bring his  crystal near to historia's location and  at that point he just needs to sit back  and wait for things to play out days  later when levi eventually beheads the  beast's titan and brings the rumbling to  a stop that would be aaron's signal to  exit his shell and make contact with the  royal baby this fresh contact with the  titan of royal blood would once again  give him access to the coordinate and i  reckon there are two main things he'd  want to do number one the colossal  titans would begin marching forward  again as he restarts the rumbling and  number two he'd bring his friends into  pass to explain the situation aaron  would have to make it super clear that  although he gave him the freedom to try  and stop him in this reality there's  nothing left they can do to actually win  that's why he'd offer everyone in the  alliance the chance to return to the  island where they can continue their  lives or even start a whole new life  without the fear of being hunted down by  mali  over the next couple days a hundred  percent of the world's population would  then be eradicated leaving a planet  where only the alien empire exists mass  murder on this scale is something the  alliance obviously wanted to avoid but  for the people on the island they'd be  on the side of the egress and would  worship aaron is the closest thing they  have to a god from a purely political  standpoint i think most people would  want him to become the new ruler of  elder which is something flock outright  stated during the final season however  aaron has never had that kind of  ambition and instead i think his main  focus would be rebuilding his broken  relationships this is what brings us to  how the titan curse would come to an end  in the anime original timeline because  if aaron is going to survive in this  universe the curse has to disappear one  way or another if we examine the manga  timeline for a sec the reason time  powers seemingly disappeared wasn't just  because aaron was killed but rather it  was because aaron was killed by mikasel  while the founder was watching his death  under those specific circumstances is  what ended the curse of emir cause ymir  saw that mikasa was able to let the  person she loves die something the  founder herself was never able to do in  yamir's mind the concept of love was  intertwined with the idea of her being a  slave and fritz being the master meaning  she always did what he wanted even if  that meant making titans for two  thousand years however by mikasa being  able to kill the man she loved ymir  learnt that breaking free from her slave  mindset is possible and that was the  true cause of the titan curse  disappearing therefore for the tying  curse to disappear in the anime timeline  it's crucial that ymir learns this same  lesson but without someone having to  kill aaron the way i see it there's very  few ways that can happen especially  considering that mikasa still loves him  regardless of whether he's a mass  murderer bearing that in mind there's  almost nothing aaron could do that would  make mikasa willingly turn her back on  him which is i guess what would have to  happen in this timeline for the founder  to find peace however after thinking  about it for a while i did come up with  one controversial thing that has the  potential to make this a reality and  that's if aaron is really the father of  historia's baby if something like that  was to be confirmed it might just be  enough to force mikisa to move on  because she feel betrayed on like a  million different levels when it comes  to emir she often saw fritz with other  women and it's heavily implied she never  had the courage to do or say anything  about it so if mikasa was to react by  leaving aaron forever then amazingly  that could be enough to eradicate the  power of the titans ultimately the only  way to remove the curse of emir is for  your mere spirit to be at peace and if  the only way she can find peace is by  learning these lessons through mikasa  then this is the way it has to be  honestly i do wish there was a better  way that time powers could disappear but  based on the ending we got in the manga  this was the most logical method that  didn't involve eren dying or mikasa  dying of course a sad consequence would  be that the original trio would be split  up forever with armin being like a  parent who has custody of mikasa during  the week and then custody of aaron every  other weekend anyhow people that was my  take on how an anime original ending  could theoretically make sense and if  you liked it then i'd appreciate if you  hit that like button and subscribe for  more videos like this  before we end today's video i wanted 